    {
      "id": "s2",
      "kind": "content",
      "heading": "A family of related molecules",
      "narration": "The word cannabinoid originally described a group of compounds found only in the cannabis plant. Chemically they are terpenophenolic compounds: each molecule combines a phenol ring, like the ones found in many plant products, with a terpene-derived portion, built from the same building blocks as the scents of pine and citrus. Most of them share a skeleton of twenty-one carbon atoms. More than one hundred different phytocannabinoids, meaning plant cannabinoids, have now been identified, and they differ from one another in small details of this common framework.",
      "bullets": [
        {
          "text": "Terpenophenolic compounds: a phenol ring plus a terpene-derived part",
          "at": 0.15
        },
        {
          "text": "Most share a 21-carbon skeleton",
          "at": 0.5
        },
        {
          "text": "More than 100 phytocannabinoids identified",
          "at": 0.65
        },
        {
          "text": "They differ in small details of a common framework",
          "at": 0.85
        }
      ],
      "visual": {
        "type": "cards",
