    {
      "id": "s4",
      "kind": "content",
      "heading": "The main phytocannabinoids",
      "narration": "A handful of phytocannabinoids are studied most. Delta nine tetrahydrocannabinol, THC, is the principal psychoactive constituent and binds to both cannabinoid receptors. Cannabidiol, CBD, has a very similar formula but a different shape; it binds only weakly to the cannabinoid receptors and interacts with several other proteins. Cannabigerol, CBG, is the neutral form of the biosynthetic starting material. Cannabichromene, CBC, and tetrahydrocannabivarin, THCV, which has a shorter side chain, are also present. Cannabinol, CBN, is not made by the plant directly; it forms when THC is oxidised during ageing.",
      "bullets": [
        {
          "text": "THC: principal psychoactive constituent; binds CB1 and CB2",
          "at": 0.1
        },
        {
          "text": "CBD: same formula, different shape; weak at CB1/CB2, other targets",
          "at": 0.33
        },
        {
          "text": "CBG: neutral form of the biosynthetic precursor",
          "at": 0.55
        },
        {
          "text": "CBC, THCV (shorter side chain); CBN forms from aged THC",
          "at": 0.7
        }
      ],
